;; AXS89 (a), the user 2026-11-10 (doc/asm/AMD64-SURVEY.md, "As built: AXS89, AXS90"; doc/GATE-SURVEY.md, GT8.4): x86i-check's programs for
;; the planner's rotation (test/gate/crops/asm.edn's :rotate on x86i-check, the part :all: the map whose :id is the part, its :subset the
;; program names, as the record test/asm/x86i-results-amd64.edn's rows x86i/NAME, decode/NAME, lockstep/NAME, step/NAME and loader/NAME
;; carry them). The subset runs every night and, alone, in the clean run's rotation tier; the rest of the 45 programs (the 12 synthetic
;; ones, test/asm/x86i/'s, test/asm/run/'s) runs a seventh a night (a program's slice: the first 8 hex digits of the SHA-256 of its name,
;; mod 7), each run `bin/repr-asm x86i-check --only LIST`, judged on what it ran, with its slice-foreign control. --full and the clean
;; run's whole tier run all of them. The subset: the quick programs (under a second of run, the step mode included), which hold the
;; subjects and references of most of the controls (test/asm/controls-x86i.txt: p4-hello, exit-status, calls, loop-sum, tls, relocs-data,
;; weak, comdat, musl-string, musl-setjmp, two-objects, string, misc); the slow ones (alu, muldiv, the synthetic families: 4 to 41 s) rotate.
;; Read with the Clojure reader.
[{:id :all
  :subset ["p4-hello" "exit-status" "calls" "loop-sum" "tls" "relocs-data" "weak" "comdat" "musl-string" "musl-setjmp"
           "two-objects" "string" "misc"]}
 ;; AXS91 (a), the user 2026-11-11: asm-amd64-encode's mc-x86 (the names bare, as the record test/asm/encode-results-amd64.edn's rows
 ;; mc-x86/NAME carry them): the subjects and references of the encode, print and cross-syntax controls (controls-encode.txt,
 ;; controls-print.txt, controls-cross.txt: also :always in the step, so every slice judges its controls) but the two heavy pairs (AVX-64 against AVX2-64 and
 ;; avx512-intel against avx512f_vl-intel: 17,000 stated encodings of the 106,000, the subset's time doubled), which run in --full's whole and the clean run's; the other files run a seventh a night
 {:id :mc-x86
  :subset ["I86-64" "I86-32" "SSE2-32" "SSE2-64" "avx512bw-64-att" "avx512dq-att"
           "avx10.2-bf16-64-intel" "avx10.2-bf16-32-intel" "apx-add-att" "apx-sub-att" "apx-ccmp-att" "apx-ctest-att" "x86-64" "avx-64-intel"]}]
